7. Mandatory Donation of Financial Proceeds

No person or entity is authorized to retain financial gain derived from an authorized fork, modification, Derivative Work, redistribution, or Commercial Use of the Software unless the Author expressly agrees otherwise in a separate written agreement.

Unless the Author expressly provides a different written arrangement, 100% of all Proceeds derived from an authorized use of the Software must be donated to a charitable, nonprofit, community, research, educational, humanitarian, or other cause selected by the Author.

The specific cause and any additional donation requirements shall be identified by the Author in the written authorization granting permission.

The recipient of the donation shall be selected solely by the Author, subject to any applicable legal requirements.

7.1 No Retention of Proceeds

The authorized user may not retain, divert, conceal, redirect, or otherwise personally benefit from any Proceeds subject to this Section.

Unless otherwise expressly agreed in writing, the donation obligation applies to 100% of the gross Proceeds attributable to the authorized use.

No deduction for personal profit, operating expenses, salaries, administrative costs, marketing expenses, or other business expenses shall reduce the amount required to be donated, except where the Author expressly agrees otherwise in writing.

7.2 Proof of Donation

Following each donation, the authorized user must provide the Author with reasonable documentary evidence establishing that the required donation was made.

Such evidence may include, as applicable:

- An official donation receipt;
- A transaction confirmation;
- A receipt issued by the receiving organization;
- A bank or payment confirmation;
- A publicly verifiable donation record; or
- Other documentation reasonably sufficient to establish the amount, recipient, and date of the donation.

Proof of donation must be sent to "fourgeailabs@gmail.com" within fourteen (14) calendar days after the donation is made, unless a different period is specified in the Author's written authorization.

The proof must reasonably identify:

a) The amount donated;

b) The date of the donation;

c) The recipient organization or cause; and

d) The transaction or confirmation identifying the donation.

The Author may reasonably request additional documentation where the information provided is insufficient to verify compliance.

